            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Personal Interests and Charities</strong><br>\nHe is well known for his interest in architecture and the built environment, organic farming, and climate change. He has published books and articles and has given speeches on these topics. His charity, The Prince's Trust, has helped over 950,000 young people.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Marriage and Family</strong><br>\nCharles's first marriage to Lady Diana Spencer in 1981 was widely publicized. They had two sons, Prince William and Prince Harry, before their divorce in 1996. In 2005, he married Camilla Parker Bowles, who became the Duchess of Cornwall. His personal life has been a subject of public fascination.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Public Perception</strong><br>\nThroughout his life, public perception of Charles has shifted. His marriage to Diana, her subsequent death, and his marriage to Camilla have been media focal points. Despite controversies, he has maintained a commitment to his roles and responsibilities as Prince of Wales.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
